From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] internet-detector: check fixes, IP version, sing-box outbound check

Fixes of the daemon (main.lua):

- URL test: curl got only --connect-timeout. A connection that is
  accepted at once (a local proxy, a transparent redirect) and then
  hangs blocked the instance for good: the status stayed as it was, in
  the "Web UI only" mode the instance did not even stop. Now --max-time
  is twice the connection timeout (at least 3 s).
- URL test: the HTTP code was taken from the first header line. Through
  an HTTP proxy that is the answer of the proxy ("200 Connection
  established"). Now the code comes from curl (-w %{http_code}).
- TCP check: only the first address of the host was tried. Now every
  address is tried until one accepts the connection.
- Values from UCI (host, device, URL, proxy user and password) went to
  /bin/sh unquoted or in double quotes: "$" or a quote in a password
  broke the command. Now they are passed in single quotes.
- The polling interval counted loop passes, not seconds: the time of
  the check itself was added to the interval. Now it counts by the
  monotonic clock from the start of a check.
- Variables leaked into the global scope ("local a = 1, b").

New options of an instance (the defaults keep the former behaviour):

- ip_family: 0 (any, default), 4 or 6 - address family of the TCP
  check, ping (-4/-6) and curl (--ipv4/--ipv6).
- http_method: head (default) or get - for servers that answer HEAD
  with 405 or 403.
- http_any_code: 1 - the URL is available on any HTTP response (default
  0: 2xx and 3xx only).
- check_type 3: delay test of sing-box outbounds through the Clash API
  (GET /proxies/<tag>/delay). Options clash_api_outbounds (list of
  tags, tried in order), clash_api_test_url, clash_api_url and
  clash_api_secret. With an empty clash_api_url the controller and the
  secret of homeproxy (infra.clash_api_controller,
  infra.clash_api_secret) are used, 0.0.0.0 replaced by 127.0.0.1.
  An outbound may also be given as the name or label of a homeproxy
  routing node or node: homeproxy names the outbound of a routing node
  after its node (cfg-<node>-out), of an urltest routing node after the
  routing node itself.

The status file gets "latency" (ms of the last successful check),
"checked" (time of the last check) and "error" (reason of the last
failure: curl or HTTP code, Clash API answer) and is written after every
check. In the "Web UI only" mode an instance exits when
/etc/config/internet-detector changes, and the next poll of the page
starts it with the new settings (before, the page kept the instances
alive with the old settings).

